
DHCP Topology, Verification & Simulation Suite

This configuration covers the network topology with a Router, Switch, DHCP Server, and 3 client PCs. It assigns the structural IP metrics and setups dynamic addressing.

1. Core Router Configuration

text
enable
configure terminal
hostname Router1

! Configure the local interface connecting to the switch
interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit
end
write memory
Use code with caution.

2. DHCP Server Configuration (Static Base)

Open the configuration properties of your DHCP Server device in Packet Tracer and input these values under the Desktop -> IP Configuration and Services -> DHCP menus:
• Interface IP Address: 192.168.10.2
• Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.0
• Default Gateway: 192.168.10.1
• DNS Server: 8.8.8.8
• DHCP Service Status: Set toggle button to ON
• Start IP Address: 192.168.10.10
• Maximum Number of Users: 41 (to cover up to .50)

🌐 Question 7: Inter-VLAN Routing (Router-on-a-Stick)

This configuration addresses the office network design containing two switches, one router, and 4 PCs distributed across VLAN 10 (Sales) and VLAN 20 (HR) using an encapsulation trunk.

1. Switch Configuration

text
enable
configure terminal
hostname Switch1

! Create the structural VLANs
vlan 10
 name Sales
exit
vlan 20
 name HR
exit

! Assign FastEthernet ports 0/1 and 0/2 to VLAN 10 (Sales)
interface range FastEthernet0/1-2
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 10
 no shutdown
exit

! Assign FastEthernet ports 0/3 and 0/4 to VLAN 20 (HR)
interface range FastEthernet0/3-4
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 20
 no shutdown
exit

! Configure interface FastEthernet 0/5 as the uplink trunk to the Router
interface FastEthernet0/5
 switchport mode trunk
 switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20
 no shutdown
exit
end
write memory
Use code with caution.

2. Router Sub-Interface Configuration

text
enable
configure terminal
hostname Router-on-a-Stick

! Bring up the main physical interface layer
interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 no shutdown
exit

! Configure Sub-interface for VLAN 10 (Sales)
interface GigabitEthernet0/0.10
 encapsulation dot1Q 10
 ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0
exit

! Configure Sub-interface for VLAN 20 (HR)
interface GigabitEthernet0/0.20
 encapsulation dot1Q 20
 ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0
exit
end
write memory
